# MoviePilot acceleration (metadata / control-plane / API only)
# Updated: 2026-08-04
#
# Consumers:
#   1. Quantumult X remote filter (force-policy=Proxy)
#   2. Server-side sing-box (ai2americaproxy) MOVIEPILOT_RULE_URL
#
# Principle: accelerate only small, latency-sensitive, blocked-in-CN traffic.
# Anything whose size is unbounded — BitTorrent, cloud drives, media streams,
# release assets, container images, OS packages — must NOT be listed here.
# See moviepilot-direct.list for the explicit never-proxy set.

# ========= MoviePilot official services =========
# API, plugin market index, site metadata.
HOST-SUFFIX,movie-pilot.org,Proxy

# ========= TMDB (primary metadata source) =========
# Covers api.themoviedb.org, www.themoviedb.org, image.tmdb.org.
# Note: image.tmdb.org carries poster/backdrop artwork and is the largest
# legitimate consumer in this file; a full library scrape can reach a few GB.
HOST-SUFFIX,themoviedb.org,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,tmdb.org,Proxy

# ========= TheTVDB =========
# Covers api4.thetvdb.com and artworks.thetvdb.com.
HOST-SUFFIX,thetvdb.com,Proxy

# ========= Fanart artwork =========
HOST-SUFFIX,fanart.tv,Proxy

# ========= Anime metadata =========
HOST-SUFFIX,anilist.co,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,trace.moe,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,bgm.tv,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,bangumi.tv,Proxy

# ========= Watchlist / subtitles =========
HOST-SUFFIX,trakt.tv,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,opensubtitles.com,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,opensubtitles.org,Proxy

# ========= GitHub: plugin market, version checks, source =========
# The suffix covers api.github.com and codeload.github.com.
# raw.githubusercontent.com is the actual plugin file-fetch path.
# Release-asset CDNs are deliberately excluded — see moviepilot-direct.list.
HOST-SUFFIX,github.com,Proxy
HOST,raw.githubusercontent.com,Proxy
HOST,gist.githubusercontent.com,Proxy

# ========= Notification channels =========
# The suffix covers api.telegram.org, including bot file uploads.
HOST-SUFFIX,telegram.org,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,t.me,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,slack.com,Proxy
HOST-SUFFIX,day.app,Proxy

# ========= Media server online endpoints (auth only, never streams) =========
# plex.tv is token/claim validation. Local streaming uses *.plex.direct,
# which is forced direct in moviepilot-direct.list.
HOST-SUFFIX,plex.tv,Proxy
# Emby Premiere key validation.
HOST-SUFFIX,mb3admin.com,Proxy

# ========= Plugin Python dependencies =========
# Wheels are a few MB each and fetched rarely. Drop these two lines if you
# point MoviePilot's PIP_PROXY at a domestic mirror instead.
HOST-SUFFIX,pypi.org,Proxy
HOST,files.pythonhosted.org,Proxy

# ========= Your own overseas PT sites (opt in per site) =========
# Site browsing and .torrent fetches are kilobyte-scale, so proxying a site
# domain is cheap. The actual BitTorrent transfer is peer traffic handled by
# qBittorrent/Transmission and never passes through this HTTP proxy.
# Add only the sites you actually use, one suffix per line, e.g.:
# HOST-SUFFIX,example-tracker.org,Proxy
#
# Before adding a site, check how its WAF treats the upstream exit. Measured on
# hdbao.cc: the US node gets `cf-mitigated: challenge` and a 403 JS interstitial
# that a scraper cannot solve, while the server's own domestic exit is waved
# straight through to /login.php. Cloudflare also binds cf_clearance to the IP
# that solved the challenge, so moving a site onto a rotating upstream node
# invalidates its cookie on every node change.
#
# So hdbao.cc is deliberately absent here. Enabling MoviePilot's per-site proxy
# still routes it through this proxy; final=direct then sends it out via the
# server's domestic IP, which is the path that actually works. Site pages and
# .torrent fetches are kilobyte-scale, so that extra hop costs nothing.
